WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.549
Easy Greek Myths. The Wooden Horse of Troy.

00:00:03.549 --> 00:00:08.054
The Greeks and the people of Troy had been at war for ten years.

00:00:08.054 --> 00:00:11.082
Troy was a strong city with high walls.

00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:16.102
The Greeks could not get in, and the people of Troy could not make them go away.

00:00:16.102 --> 00:00:19.689
Then a clever Greek named Odysseus had an idea.

00:00:19.689 --> 00:00:22.515
The Greeks built a huge horse out of wood.

00:00:22.515 --> 00:00:24.172
It was empty inside.

00:00:24.172 --> 00:00:28.935
Odysseus and some of the best Greek soldiers climbed in and hid there.

00:00:28.935 --> 00:00:32.859
The rest of the Greeks got into their ships and sailed away.

00:00:32.859 --> 00:00:34.759
But they did not go far.

00:00:34.759 --> 00:00:37.480
They hid behind an island near the coast.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.251
In the morning the people of Troy came out.

00:00:40.251 --> 00:00:41.772
The Greeks were gone!

00:00:41.772 --> 00:00:44.896
Only the great wooden horse stood on the sand.

00:00:44.896 --> 00:00:48.416
"It is a present for the gods," some of them said.

00:00:48.416 --> 00:00:50.409
"Let us bring it into the city."

00:00:50.409 --> 00:00:55.913
One old man shouted, "Do not trust the Greeks, even when they bring presents!"

00:00:55.913 --> 00:00:57.380
But nobody listened.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:59.548
They pulled the horse through the gate.

00:00:59.548 --> 00:01:04.455
Then they ate, drank and danced all day because the war was over.

00:01:04.455 --> 00:01:06.984
That night everyone slept deeply.

00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:11.647
In the middle of the night, a small door opened in the side of the horse.

00:01:11.647 --> 00:01:14.100
The Greek soldiers climbed down.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.915
They ran to the gate of the city and opened it.

00:01:16.915 --> 00:01:22.096
The Greek ships had come back in the dark, and the army was waiting outside.

00:01:22.096 --> 00:01:23.634
The Greeks ran in.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:26.666
By morning, the city of Troy was burning.

00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:28.675
The long war was over.

00:01:28.675 --> 00:01:34.303
Today, people still speak of a "Trojan horse" when a present hides a danger.
